A||||9||GT Bastard||Finally decided on a cam for my setup...||||12||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||01-17-2001||08:24 AM||||I finally decided on the Crane Compucam 2030 from Jegs.  <P>duration: 264/274<BR>lift: .423/.423<P>It's the bigger of the two cams Crane offers. I figure as long as I've got a beefed fuel system, extrude honed intake, headers, and soon to be ported heads, I should be able to put that extra cam to use.  Does this cam change the idle very noticeably?  Shall I use factory springs or use the stiffer ones I currently have? Trav knows what they are.||||reg||12
Z||000001||Steven||01-17-2001||10:31 AM||||Factory spring are only good for a max. lift of .420". Now I know it doesn't sound like much, but for the price of valve spring, it would be worth buy better spring. After all the work you are doing, it would be a shame to have the factory spring fail. On your cam spec card that came with your cam(if you haven't bought the cam, a copy of the spec card can be seen on the crane cam web site) crane recommends a valve spring, and gives you the part number 99848. FYI GM sell this spring, but puts it in one of their boxes, and sell it under the part # of 12363215. If you haven't bought your cam you might want to know that their is a bigger cam out there. GM # is 12363220. It is made for GM by Crane. The Crane # 253902. It's specs are :<BR>          <BR>Dur. @.050 204/216  int/exh<BR>Lift      .427/.454 int/exh<P>Hope this info helps.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||01-17-2001||05:44 PM||||Hey GT Bastard, What is the displacement of your engine? Is it 2.8 or 3.1-liters? <P>That GM 12363220 camshaft is a better camshaft for the 3.1,3.4-liter engines than the Crane 2030 is. The GM camshaft makes as much bottom end power as the Crane 2030 camshaft but the GM 12363220 camshaft makes more top-end power.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||01-17-2001||05:45 PM||||Thanks for the info...  I already ordered the cam, but it's not here yet.  I woulda gone for the GM cam, but it's too much money.||||reg||1
Z||000004||GT Bastard||01-17-2001||05:48 PM||||It's a 3.2 btw||||reg||1
Z||000005||N_Man||01-17-2001||07:53 PM||||Ive got that cam on a 2.8 and the idle is fine.<P>Im using comp cams springs packaged for a SBC, the set of 16 was like 70 CDN. less than any performance set for the V6.<P>The cam is actually a pretty good choice, It REALLY helps the top end.  And use the stiffer springs||||reg||1
Z||000006||lou_dias||01-18-2001||12:47 PM||||I have that damn Crane .423/.423 cam in my GT...  Return it.  Get something with more lift that maked power to 5000 rpm.  This one dies to quickly after 4500...  The extra displacement will make up for any loss in torque from the higher revving cam.<P>My last cam in my 3.3 had .434/.454 lift.  It was from Associated Auto...  Definitely peppier than this one in my 3.4 rebuild.<P>||||reg||1
